fail "string push generic", "7:1: `put[Float]` cannot use `T = Float`: the generic body applies `push` to `T`, which `Float` does not support"
  # A type parameter given to `push[T, e]` must be an integer in every instance.

  sub put[T](t: !String, v: T)
    !t.push[T, .big](v)

  s = String()
  put(!s, 1.5)

